i hope they are right he should not have  lived this long  his other family members wanted to see  him dead from the moment that he was  born but jaime was the only one who was  always there  he was the only one who never looked at  him as if he were some kind of a monster  and i can understand why he would want  to set his brother free even if it meant  his own life  i think most of us would try to do the  same thing for someone we really loved  not to mention he was really counting on  the fact that jaime would change his  mind and do the right thing by making  sure the city surrendered before  everyone had to die  now this is something tyrion will have  to answer for later  the unsullied men who were guarding  jaime know that it was tyrion who saw  him last  it will be fairly obvious that he was  the one that set jaime free  now i wonder if davos will have to  answer for this because he is the one  who made sure jaime got off dragonstone  and back over to king's landing  he may have to face consequences as well  and right now  danny's not in a very good mood now  let's get to the scenes in king's  landing  when everyone was getting into position  it felt very intense and i absolutely  loved it  the shots of king's landing looked  amazing euron's fleet out on the  blackwater bay looked amazing  the golden company marching down the  streets looked badass  then we saw arya and the hound moving  around the city trying to get to the red  keep  then we had jaime moving around the city  trying to get to the red keep  i was on the edge of my seat during the  whole time i kept thinking who's gonna  get the cersei first who's gonna get the  cersei first will it be danny  arya jamie who knows but i can't wait to  see what happens next  then we saw the golden company line up  right outside of the city gate  i could not wait to see how well they  could fight because we kept here and  cersei has 20 000 mercenaries who are  well trained  and well rested they even showed harry  