ld win even  after she saw how bad things were  getting  i almost started to laugh when she said  that city will not fall  the red keep has never fell i could not  tell if she was just very confident or  if she was in denial  or maybe a little bit of both anyways  now let's get to what everyone is  talking about  the moment in which daenerys decides to  turn king's landing into a living hell  the bells begin to ring but daenerys is  not satisfied by their easy surrender  this causes dany to snap you see dany  gave cersei the opportunity to surrender  before anyone had to die but cersei did  not accept  now king's landing is surrendering  almost immediately  which dany most likely feels like  missandei and rhaegal died for nothing  why did that have to happen if they were  just going to give up so easily  then you add to that all the other  losses dany has had to face  and all the characters around her trying  to cause her downfall  so she loses it and i have to say i was  absolutely shocked by this  not because danny turned into a mad  queen that has been a theory for over a  decade i always knew that could happen  but what i was not expecting is how  relentless danny was  after she lost it danny was burning the  civilians for  almost 30 minutes of the episode or  that's at least what it felt like  i remember very late into the episode  when it felt like it was over  i thought she has to be done there is no  way she is still burning everything  then the scene cuts back to danny's  dragon still burning the streets and i  was like holy [ __ ] will this ever stop  now i was hoping that danny would burn  all of cersei's soldiers  i was hoping that danny would burn down  the red key i was even ready to accept a  little bit of collateral damage but this  i cannot accept  and i don't care how upset danny was you  cannot justify those actions  i even saw some fans say well they all  deserved it  they were cheering for ned stark to get  executed well there is maybe only a few  hundred at ned's execution  and most of them were adults danny was  killing children who weren't even alive  when ned was executed  now imagine if that were you and your  child out there running on the streets  would you think you deserved to die just  because you lived in that city  i don't think so and yes she was killing  them intentionally  that was not collateral damage that was  murder  now on the other hand it absolutely felt  rushed  yes danny has shown some signs of  madness before but nothing like this  i think if they did want to have danny  do something like that then we should  have seen her kill some innocent  civilians on smaller scales leading up  to this  every other time dany burnt someone  alive it felt justified  i don't think it would have been as  shocking if we seen danny target some  civilians in other smaller battles  before this big one  now if i take a step back and just look  at it as someone who likes to watch  television  it looked incredible getting to see that  kind of chaos in king's landing makes  for one hell of an episode  like i said i was on the edge of my seat  the entire time i also did like how we  were able to see the wildfire getting  set off during the scenes of the battle  danny and bran's visions also came true  like most of us knew they would  the dragon flew over king's landing and  the red keep was  massacred but then we see a lame ass  euron and jaime fight on the beach  the only thing i really liked about the  scene was when it reminded me of what  jaime once said to ned stark back in the  first season  so will you tell yourself at night  you're a servant of justice that you  were avenging my father when you shove  your sword in aries targaryen's back  tell me if i stab the mad king in the  belly instead of the back  would you admire me more when they were  talking about jaime killing the mad king  jaime said something along the lines of  would you have admired me more  if i stabbed the mad king in the belly  instead of the back  i don't know if this was meant to be a  call back or not but it did work for me  because the fatal blow was when jaime  stabbed euron in the belly  i also did really like when the hound  was finally able to fight his brother  this was very predictable but it was  also very satisfying for me  now right before that does happen arya  and the hound do have a nice final  moment together  i kind of saw this as the hound making  arya realize getting your revenge is not  worth your own life  you really don't want to live your  entire life where you're only motivated  by hate  and wanting to get that revenge against  those who have done you or your family  wrong  cersei was about to die anyway so why  stay here to kill her when it's going to  cost you your own life  now it was very interesting when we saw  the mountain no longer wanting to obey  cersei or qyburn's commands the  clegane's hatred for one another runs so  deep that not even his masters could  contain him i do kind of wish that we  would have got to see cersei's head  slam against the rock just like qyburn's  that would have been a hell of a lot  more satisfying than seeing her have the  chance to run  right back into jaime's arms again i  can't even begin to tell you how  disappointed i was when cersei lannister  died the way that she did  for everything that she has done and  caused over the years i really wanted to  see her suffer for it  anyways for a few moments i wasn't sure  if the hound was going to win the fight  or not  his brother was almost able to do the  same finishing move that he did to ober  martel  now what's kind of funny is the hound  actually got the upper hand by doing  what arya once said she would do to him  he stuck the blade right through his eye  and out the back of his skull  someday i'm gonna put a sword through  your eye and out the back of your skull  and of course speaking of arya stark the  episode more or less ends with her  running through the streets trying to  find some cover  she does try to help a mother and her  daughter get to safety but danny runs  both of them down in the street  i'm sure most of you noticed this  already but the little girl was holding  a white horse in her hand  and interestingly enough it's a white  horse that somehow appears out of  nowhere to give arya a ride out of the  city  now arya does see the mother and the  child again but they were burned alive  the horse in her hand is also very  reminiscent of the one that davos gave  to shireen baratheon  when it comes to the white horse i think  most would agree that it most likely  represents death  which does fit with arya's star given  her storyline throughout most of the  show not only her time with the faceless  men  but also the phrase what do we say to  the god of death not today  now does it mean that arya stark will  take that white horse to go kill danny  some say that she does have green eyes  so maybe arya kills her for burning  everyone in the city  well we know that arya could kill dany  if she really wanted to but i think  someone else will kill danny before it's  all said and done  most of you already know who that is  i'll just leave it at that because i  don't want to spoil it for others who  may not want to know  anyways that's all i really have to say  about this episode comment down below  and let me know what you think  i want to thank everyone for watching  the video and i also want to thank  everyone for supporting the channel  i hope you all have a great day i'll see  you again very soon bye  [Music]  so  you
 

